In this setting, early predictive biomarkers of response are needed. 
The Early Regression Index (ERI) [9,10] integrates volumetric changes 
in the gross tumour volume (GTV) between simulation and the tenth 
treatment fraction. The prospective single-centre THUNDER-2 trial 
evaluated ERI-guided MRI-based adaptive RT: patients with ERI > 13.1 
(“non-responders”) received an adaptive boost to 60.1 Gy to the residual 
primary tumour using MRI-LINAC technology [11]. The aim of this 
study was to evaluate the feasibility, safety, and clinical impact of this 
strategy in patients predicted to have a low probability of complete 
response.
2. Materials and methods
2.1. Study design and patient selection
The THUNDER-2 protocol is a prospective, interventional, single- 
centre phase II trial (NCT04815694), approved by the Ethics Commit-
tee of the Fondazione Policlinico Universitario “A. Gemelli” IRCCS of 
Rome, Italy (IC 3460) [12]. Enrollment spanned from March 2021 to 
March 2024. Written informed consent was obtained from all patients 
prior to enrollment. Patients underwent long-course preoperative che-
moradiotherapy on a 0.35T MRI-LINAC system (MRIdian, ViewRay Inc., 
Mountain View, CA, USA) in supine position. Simulation included MRI 
and CT acquisition with rigid co-registration for treatment planning. 
TRUFI MRI was used for setup verification, contouring, and adaptive 
planning. Target delineation followed institutional guidelines [13]. 
Clinical Target Volume 1 (CTV1) encompassed the primary tumour and 
corresponding mesorectum (high-dose target), while CTV2 included the 
entire mesorectum and pelvic lymphatic drainage (elective volume). 
Planning Target Volume 1 (PTV1) and PTV2 were generated by applying 
5-mm isotropic expansions. A simultaneous integrated boost (SIB) 
approach was used, delivering 55 Gy to PTV1 and 45 Gy to PTV2 in 25 
fractions (2.2 and 1.8 Gy per fraction, respectively) [10]. GTV delinea-
tion was validated by a second radiation oncologist.
ERI was calculated at the tenth fraction, according to this formula 
[10,11]: 
ERI=␀ ln
