neutrophils within irradiated tumors remained unchanged, whereas a 
significant increase in CXCR2 expression was observed in bone marrow 
neutrophils from irradiated mice. This finding is consistent with previ-
ous reports and suggests that radiotherapy may promote neutrophil 
mobilization by upregulating CXCR2 expression at the source [42]. 
