Fig. 1. Some mechanisms of TME in terms of lung cancer metastasis. A. Lactic acid can induce the polarization of TAMs toward type M2 and the reduction of 
ATP6V0d2 expressed in TAMs, and has a positive effect on the remodeling of ECM and the development of EMT. B. Hypoxia causes glycolysis and enhances glucose 
uptake in LUAD cells to help tumor progression. C. IL-6 activates STAT1/ZEB2-AS1 and induces the self-renewal of CD133 (+) cells and the production of TIM-4. D. 
CAFs release inflammatory cytokines, VCAM-1, and also play roles in the degradation and remodeling of ECM, EMT, and angiogenesis. E. WDFY2 interacts with 
VAMP3 to control the generation of MMP14 and reduce the degradation of ECM, thus inhibiting tumor cell invasion. F. MiR-210 released by exosomes causes CAFs to 
release angiogenesis factors. G. APP on tumor cells binds to DR6 on endothelial cells to ensure that tumor cells can leave blood vessels and cause proliferation. 
