by STK11 phenotype or mutation status across cohorts
(Supplementary Fig. 20 ). Taken together, our results
suggest that STK11-def tumors are resistant to ICB
because of dysfunction of the CD8 þ T-cells that might
not be reversible by ICB alone, rather than relying solely
on T-cell exclusion.
Discussion
Previous work from our and other groups has reported
the use of genomic proﬁling in identifying determinants of
ICB response or resistance in NSCLC. 6,55 Particular
emphasis has been placed on the detrimental impacts of
STK11 mutations 6– 8,48 and the co-occurring mutation
