0.72–0.86) and moderate correlations with HBI and MUST. The LBP/albumin ratio showed the strongest clinical correlations of any biomarker (HBI ρ = 0.41; MUST 
ρ = 0.50; BMI ρ = ␀ 0.46; all P < 0.001). Abbreviations: LBP, lipopolysaccharide-binding protein; IL, interleukin; CRP, C-reactive protein; CAR, CRP-to-albumin ratio; 
