Conclusion
This study utilized the SEER database to longitudinally assess the
impact of radiotherapy on the risk of Secondary Primary Lung Cancer
(SPLC) in elderly female breast cancer survivors. Findings indicate that
patientswhounderwentradiotherapyexhibiteda31%increasedriskof
developing SPLC compared to those who did not receive radiotherapy.
Despite the increased incidence of SPLC, the survival rates were not
significantlyimpacted,suggestingthatwhileradiotherapyraisestherisk
of secondary malignancies, it does not detrimentally affect overall sur-
vival. This underscores the necessity for rigorous risk management and
continuous monitoring of breast cancer survivors who receive
radiotherapy.
