to 20% of control cells (p < 0.05) ( Figure S5D).
As expected, ENZ treatment repressed AR signaling in LNCaP
(p < 0.0001) and, notably, also repressed AR signaling in
LNCaPRB1/C0//C0;TP53/C0//C0DKO cells (p < 0.0001) ( Figure 6E). No sig-
niﬁcant upregulation of a NE expression program was evident in
LNCaPRB1/C0//C0;TP53/C0//C0DKO cells treated with ENZ ( Fig-
ure 6 F). Reﬂecting repression of growth, the CCP score of
LNCaPRB1/C0//C0;TP53/C0//C0DKO cells was reduced by ENZ (p =
