ATR function may be particularly effective. Cells with TP53/RB1
loss upregulate CHK1 and are dependent on ATR/CHK1
signaling to suppress CDC25A-C-mediated CCP in order to
repair replication-mediated breaks, and accordingly, ATR inhib-
itors have been shown to induce apoptosis in TP53/RB1-null
cells ( Doerr et al., 2017 ). The combined loss of TP53 and
RB1 may, consequently, confer an attractive therapeutic index
for PARP-, ATR-, and CHK1-directed therapeutics.
