3.3. Plastic strain damage model based on weibull
distribution
The constitutive equation of damaged solidiﬁed soil (Ds0) can
be derived from the constitutive relationship of nondestruc-
tive solidiﬁed soil (D ¼ 0), and the effective stress after damage
can replace the nominal stress without damage [ 54].
The solidiﬁed soil is composed of a variety of materials, a
large number of pores and cracks are randomly distributed
throughout. The characteristics of the Weibull statistical dis-
tribution are consistent with the micro-element strength of
solidiﬁed soil [ 55,56]. With the increase of strain, there are
more micro-units of internal damage of solidiﬁed soil. The
damage variable can be expressed by Eq. (11) [57].
