the content of the alkali activator simultaneously promoted
the dissolution rate of the GGBS [ 60], resulting in an increase
in cross-linking chain reaction products that ultimately
improved the compactness of the solidiﬁed soil samples. The
peak strength decreased with an increasing modulus, and the
plastic characteristics increased gradually, as shown in
Fig. 8 (h). This may be because a lower modulus resulted in
higher alkalinity, which accelerated the dissolution of GGBS
and formed a relatively stable structure of Si eOeAl and
SieOeSi [ 2], thus improving the cohesion between soil parti-
