modulus was 1.9. However, the change in the trend for Ud was
not signiﬁcant, as shown in Fig. 9 (h). This is because an in-
crease in the modulus reduced the pH value of the geopolymer
and solubility of the GGBS, producing fewer gelling products,
such as C-A-S-H [ 61]. Finally, the cementation force between
the soil particles was relatively weak and became destroyed
