absorption energy of the solidiﬁed soil was reduced. It can be
concluded that the low-modulus alkali activator and cement,
GGBS, and alkali-activator contents signiﬁcantly increased the
total absorption and elastic strain energies of solidiﬁed soil.
This study explored the damage using the ratio of Ud to U to
accurately evaluate the change rule of the dissipated energy
under different proportions of solidiﬁed soil. The energy was
dissipated during fracture initiation, propagation, and plastic
deformation in which the solidiﬁed soil increased inversely
