The dissipation energy ratio of the solidiﬁed soil exhibited an
increasing trend with an increase in the modulus ( Fig. 10 (h)).
The dissipation energy ratio increased more quickly when the
modulus increased between 0.7 and 1.1. The growth rate
decreased when the modulus was between 1.1 and 1.5. The
dissipation energy ratio increased sharply when the modulus
was 1.5. A declining trend in the dissipated energy ratio of
each fraction of the solidiﬁed soil as the curing age increased
is shown in Fig. 10. Based on the aforementioned ﬁndings, the
