increased with the Ca/Al in the reaction system. This
encouraged the polymerization of GGBS and produced more
C-A-S-H, which clearly ﬁlled the medium and large pores of
the solidiﬁed soil. The mesopores and macropores diminished
as the alkali-activator concentration increased, whereas the
micropores expanded ( Fig. 16 (c)). An increase in the alkali
activator increased the %Na 2O (the proportion of Na 2O con-
tent in the mix proportion) in the reaction system, thus pro-
moting the formation of C-A-S-H. Moreover, the increase in
OH/C0 in the alkali activator led to a reaction with carbon di-
