body part [10]. Benign tumors have several types. First is Lipoma - an 
increase of fat cells in the body in the form of cluster form found in the 
skin and underlying muscle layer is known as Lipoma—Myeloma - 
increased muscle cells in the body, which is known as myeloma. 
Myeloma is a cancer of the plasma cells. Myeloma is known as multiple 
myeloma. Fibromass - increases fibrous cells of the body.it is mainly 
found in women’s uterus. Malignant tumor - A malignant tumor is a 
dangerous cancer because it is a transferable cancer. It is transferred 
from one body part to another body part. It is not localized cancer. It has 
a metastasis process. It has several types. Carcinomas, Sarcomas, 
Leukaemia, Lymphomas. Carcinomas - Carcinomas are known as skin 
cancer. It is present in endodermal and ectodermal tissues on the surface 
of the skin. It is found on the upper surface of the skin [11]. It is a 
transferable cancer. It transfers from one cell to another cell. Sarcomas 
cancer - Sarcomas cancer is a Bone cancer.it is present in the bones of the 
