mutations were prognostic in lung cancer. Also, our MALDI and
CyCIF data were not obtained from consecutive sections of tu-
mor material, which limits our conclusions by preventing direct
comparisons between these two data types. We also did not
perform CyCIF using all possible markers informative for lung
cancer for technical reasons reﬂecting as-yet incomplete valida-
tion of antibodies for analysis of lung tissue. Additional data of
this type might be helpful in delineating mechanisms of treatment
response and resistance if applied to patient cohorts treated with
different treatment modalities. Of particular interest would be a
careful characterization of tumor-immune interactions as well
as spatial localizations of neoantigens in patients treated with
immunotherapy.
