This chapter utilises the datasets developed in Chapter Three over the
MQTT and UDP protocols in 5G H-IoT systems. The TCN model is trained
using both datasets to perform DDoS detection and mitigation. The model
uses monitoring frequency to accurately identify malicious nodes, while a
dynamic threshold mechanism is applied during the mitigation phase to
blacklist them. It achieves high prediction and mitigation accuracy across
MQTT and UDP-based datasets, outperforming conventional deep learning
models such as BiLSTM and CNN.
