• Chapter Five is based on the journal publication Akhi, M., Eising, C.
and Dhirani, L.L., 2026. Securing IoT using Lightweight TCN for Edge
Deployment on Raspberry Pi 4 IEEE Open Journal of the Communications
Society, 7, pp. 442-460.
This chapter introduces lightweight TCN-based edge deployment for detect-
ing DDoS attacks on Raspberry Pi 4 in H-IoT environments. The previously
developed MQTT and UDP-based datasets are utilised to convert the model
into TFLite format and optimise it through quantisation, reducing model
size, inference latency, and power consumption. The study demonstrates
the feasibility of deploying efficient, lightweight deep learning models on
resource-constrained edge devices to secure H-IoT systems.
• Chapter Six is based on the journal publication Akhi, M., Eising, C. and
Dhirani, L.L., 2026. Residual temporal CNNs for emerging cyber threat
detection in healthcare IoT. Discover Internet of Things .
This chapter presents a Res-TCN model for classifying multiple concur-
rent cyber threats in H-IoT systems. A realistic simulation is developed
to model normal and attack scenarios involving SF, MITM, and DDoS be-
haviours. The resulting dataset is used to train the proposed Res-TCN
model, which combines residual and temporal learning components to en-
hance classification accuracy and stability. To address class imbalance and
improve model generalisation, SMOTE is used during training. The study
presents an efficient multiclass detection framework suitable for real-time,
resource-constrained H-IoT environments.
• Chapter Seven presents concluding remarks and highlights potential di-
rections for future research.
