lated H-IoT devices, the COOJA simulation can even construct attack scenarios
to uncover cybersecurity vulnerabilities within H-IoT networks.
Hence, ML and DL techniques have been explored to prevent routing attacks
on H-IoT networks. By reviewing examples, it becomes apparent that artificial in-
telligence models significantly defend against routing attacks in 5G-IoT e-health.
COOJA has also been demonstrated to collect data from H-IoT devices.
2.7 ML-Driven Intrusion and Event Detection
in H-IoT
To ensure data security within the H-IoT, it is necessary to explore a variety of
strategic mechanisms. The section endeavours to illustrate the pivotal role of
ML in establishing and reinforcing robust security protocols in healthcare, gener-
alised ML techniques, and exploring potential cybersecurity applications. Follow-
ing this, the discussion discusses how feature extraction is essential to identifying
threats accurately and mitigating risks. Afterwards, intrusion and event detec-
tion systems designed for healthcare environments will be offered, emphasising
mechanisms for identifying potential breaches. A discourse on the reliability of
H-IoT systems is required to achieve consistent and reliable risk mitigation. The
last topic of this section is the potential and challenges associated with CNNs in
the context of IoT security.
2.7.1 ML Techniques in H-IoT Cybersecurity
The ML method involves using data and algorithms to create models replicat-
ing human learning processes. ML algorithms can be refined and optimised by
improving an algorithm’s loss function [238]. As depicted in Figure 2.12, ML is
traditionally classified into three categories: supervised, unsupervised, and rein-
forcement learning [239],[240].
Over the past several years, ML techniques have been successfully applied to
a diverse spectrum of cybersecurity challenges [241]. In the specialised domain of
H-IoT cybersecurity, these techniques have emerged as key assets, significantly en-
hancing the security level of healthcare devices and systems [242]. As illustrated
