3.8 Conclusion
This chapter presents two synthetic DDoS datasets, UL-ECE-MQTT-DDoS-H-
IoT2025 and UL-ECE-UDP-DDoS-H-IoT2025, that enable realistic traffic anal-
ysis in H-IoT environments. The datasets are generated using Cooja and ns-
3 simulators to represent application-layer (MQTT) and transport-layer (UDP)
behaviours under both normal and attack conditions. Each dataset includes
communication-level parameters such as message frequency, transmission inter-
vals, and node activity, providing a realistic representation of DDoS patterns
in heterogeneous H-IoT networks. These datasets address a key research gap
by providing domain-specific resources for evaluating data-driven cybersecurity
mechanisms in healthcare-oriented IoT systems.
