The average inference latency on the Raspberry Pi 4 is 0.70 ms per sam-
ple, as computed using (5.1) and reported in Table 5.12. This corresponds to a
maximum theoretical throughput of approximately 1429 samples per second on
a single device. Such latency enables near real-time packet-level inference at the
