(e.g., a hospital access point, home IoT hub, or 6LoWPAN border router) [466].
Additionally, prior studies demonstrate that realistic home-care and H-IoT de-
ployments often rely on a limited number of sensors (e.g., approximately 24–28
motion sensors) to enable accurate monitoring of daily living activities [467],
[468]. As a result, this research adopts a realistic scale with a limited number
of nodes to emulate H-IoT settings. It also aligns with the practical limits of
203

