IoT devices transmit data based on speciﬁc behaviours. We disDnguish between two modes of data 
transmission and two modes of transmission periodicity: Open-close and Always-open for transmission 
modes, and ConCnuous and IntermiDent for periodicity. In the Open-close mode, the device establishes 
a new connecDon with the cloud each Dme it needs to send telemetry data, transmits the data, and 
then closes the connecDon. In contrast, the Always-open mode involves the device opening a single, 
persistent connecDon with the cloud at the start and maintaining it by periodically sending telemetry 
data and keep-alive messages. For transmission periodicity, the ConCnuous mode means the device 
conDnuously transmits telemetry data at regular intervals without interrupDon. In the IntermiDent 
mode, the device alternates between acDve and inacDve periods. During acDve periods, data is 
transmi]ed similarly to the ConDnuous mode, whereas during inacDve periods, only background traﬃc 
is transmi]ed, with no telemetry data. Fig. 2 and Fig. 3 illustrate the heterogeneity of the IoT network. 
 
