Table I is operationally important because it defines how
the benchmark judges behavior. A blocked write is not treated
as a generic failure if the task oracle expects a guarded
denial, while a reconnect path is evaluated through the same
outer structure as a healthy read. This is the main reason the
paper can compare three different protocol families without
pretending they expose the same payload model.
