2) Entrance and Exit Gate Management: When a car comes
towards the entrance, an IR-sensor detects that there is a
vehicle. A buzzer goes off, notifying the car park attendant that
a vehicle is wanting access to said area. Fig. Fig.7(c) illustrates
the implementation of a servo motor acting as an exit gate
using an IR sensor [30]. At the entrance, there is an OLED
display with how many slots exist in total and available for a
car to park before it, which dynamically updates upon coming
vehicles. Fig. 7(d) shows the number of all slots offered by
