4.5. MATLAB–Based Analysis Pipeline
All post–processing was automated using MATLAB R2023b scripts to ensure reproducibil-
ity:
• Single–session analysis: analyze_psk.m and analyze_dsekp.m cleaned logs, cor-
rected NTP offsets, and computed latency distributions (mean, p95, p99).
• Multi–session analysis:Verified reliability and init–ack success across 20–30 random
resets using session counters.
• Comparativeanalysis: compare_psk_vs_dsekp.mgeneratedCDFs, boxplots, payload
histograms, and summary tables from identical datasets.
Metrics included mean/median latency, packets–per–second (PPS), bits–per–second (BPS),
payload overhead (%), packet loss, and duplicates. Statistical significance was evaluated via
two–samplet–tests, Wilcoxon rank–sum tests, and Cohen’sdeffect size.
4.6. Experimental Integrity and Reproducibility
To ensure validity and repeatability of the experiments, several controls were enforced
throughout the study:
• Identical hardware, firmware, and network configurations were used for both PSK and
DSEKP evaluations to guarantee fair comparison.
• Device clocks were synchronized via NTP before each run to ensure consistent timestamp
alignment between client and edge server.
• To ensure reliability and statistical validity, each protocol configuration (PSK and
DSEKP) was executed in a continuous session transmitting approximately 6,500 en-
crypted packets under identical conditions. Additional shorter runs were conducted
at random intervals to verify consistency and session rekeying reliability after device
resets or environmental variations. While not strictly averaged across multiple identical
trials, the large packet count and repeated random sampling ensured stable latency and
throughput statistics representative of steady-state operation.
•Outliers exceeding 10s latency (<0.05% of total samples) were excluded according to
the filtering rule in the MATLAB analysis scripts.
• Docker container images ( eclipse-mosquitto:2.0 and the custom
dsekp_aesgcm_edge build) and corresponding SHA256 hashes were archived
for version tracking.
• The full ESP32 firmware (DSEKP_Client.ino) and Python edge server source (app.py)
will be made available by the authors upon reasonable request to support reproducibility
and further research.
All experimental datasets, analysis scripts, and container definitions are referenced under the
Data Availabilitystatement to support verification and reuse by future researchers.
This setup provides a fully reproducible foundation for the comparative analysis presented
in Section 5.
