D. Performance
Table II shows the performance indicators of the proposed
CPS. The maximum steady-state synchronization error of
0.12◦ and the minimum and average round-trip latency are
431 ms and 563 ms, respectively.
The measured latencies exceed the 250 ms usability
threshold adopted in the authors’ earlier CPMT work [3]
and are an order of magnitude above the MQTT latencies
reported for teleoperation in [12], which indicates that the
protocol is not the limiting factor. The dominant term is
the polling interval of the controller loop program. The
consequence is that the system does not support continuous
motion streaming or direct manual control: at these latencies
the operator is necessarily in a move-and-wait regime, the
classical response to transmission delay in teleoperation [23].
