D. Human response time assessment
Would issuing warnings to pedestrians help reduce users’
response time and increase their safety awareness? To test
this hypothesis, we designed virtual reality (VR) experiments
in Unity3D [18], where warnings are provided via voice and
text displayed on the VR headset Meta Quest 3. There are
two traffic scenarios, one involving an interaction between the
participant (i.e., a pedestrian) and an oncoming scooter, and
the other between the participant and an oncoming vehicle. In
each scenario, participants first receive no warning and then a
