Table 3: Image Transmission Process Step
Step Description
1 - Initial Image Transmission The ImageSender receives the image from an Asset, and the ImageSplit-
ter partitions it into smaller fragments. A hash_f ile and a metadata
header are generated and transmitted via the SendHeader topic. The
FileStatusManager assigns the status ""pending"" to the hash_f ile. If no
confirmation is received, the header is retransmitted.
2 - Header Reception The ImageReceiver extracts the hash_f ile and updates its status to
""working"". The hash_f ile is returned via the hash_sender topic,
signaling successful reception.
3 - Confirmation and
Transmission of Parts Upon confirmation, the ImageSender verifies the hash_f ile status. If
accepted, image fragments are transmitted via the hash_sender_orq
topic. If rejected, no fragments are sent.
4 - Reception of Parts and
Attempted Assembly The ImageReceiver attempts to reconstruct the image using theImageRe-
store module. Missing fragments trigger Step 5.
5 - Request for Missing Parts The ImageReceiver requests missing fragments via the hash_sender
topic, specifying the hash_f ile and identifiers of the missing parts.
6 - Resending Missing Parts The ImageSender retransmits missing fragments via the
hash_sender_orq topic. Steps 4 to 6 repeat until successful re-
construction.
7 - Successful Assembly Signal Upon successful reconstruction, the ImageReceiver signals completion
by transmitting the hash_f ile via the hash_sender topic. The FileSta-
tusManager updates the status to ""completed"".
8 - Finalization and Cleanup The ImageSender verifies the status as ""completed"" and deletes tempo-
rary files to conclude the process.
