than a threshold applied at the VLM output stage. This
design choice is deliberate: a high-confidence detection can
still exhibit significant ground-plane reprojection error if the
object geometry is complex or the camera angle is shallow;
conversely, a moderate-confidence detection may project
accurately when the geometry is simple. Becauseα j alone
cannot determine the appropriate spatial safety buffer, it
must be combined with the geometric reprojection quality at
the conversion stage. Schema validation is applied to every
VLM JSON output before it propagates further; malformed,
incomplete, or internally inconsistent outputs are discarded
