ics and Artificial Intelligence from the Univer-
sity of Siegen, Germany. He is currently pursu-
ing the Ph.D. degree in Cyber-Physical Systems
with the Professorship of Cyber-Physical Systems
(Heilbronn), Department of Computer Engineer-
ing, TUM School of Computation, Information
and Technology, Technische Universität München
(TUM), Germany. His doctoral research spans machine learning, multi-
