8 Prototype Implementation & Evaluation
We evaluated our Rust core orchestrator (‘tip-core‘) and C++ edge node (‘tip-edge-cpp‘ / ‘libsodium‘ [23])
on a testbed of Raspberry Pi 4 nodes and Windows gateways. The cryptographic execution times under
varying payload sizes are shown in Figure 2.
Figure 2: Cryptographic execution times under varying payload sizes.
Our evaluation focused on matching overhead and runtime sandbox execution speed:
• Scoring Performance:Intent matching and scoring for 10,000 nodes completed in 12.4ms (as
illustrated in Figure 3).
• Translation Latency:Executing Celsius-to-Fahrenheit translation inside the ‘wasmtime‘ engine
required an average of 84𝜇s, including memory-copy overhead.
• Cryptographic Overhead:Ephemeral X25519 exchanges required 412𝜇s, while ChaCha20-
Poly1305 payload encryption remained sub-microsecond.
