Table III shows the importance of GPUs in reducing rede-
ployment time for efficient model deployment. Many base sta-
tions lack GPU functionality, causing delays in pilot jamming
detection. Transitioning to a DT environment with GPU support
can cut deployment time by 87%, minimizing downtime during
jamming attacks. The capability of DT-emulated datasets in
training models for diverse wireless spectra enhances rede-
ployment effectiveness, significantly boosting threat detection
against adaptable adversaries.
VI. C ONCLUSIONS
In this paper, we introduced TwiNet, a novel approach for
synchronizing the real and digital worlds via the MQTT pro-
tocol. Our framework enables scalable employment of DTs,
showcased in applications such as traffic monitoring, network
management, and pilot jamming prevention. TwiNet effectively
mitigates cellular network outages by adjusting packet trans-
mission while maintaining reasonable data rates. Future work
will expand on resource-intensive implementations.
