5 ACCESS CONTROL
Providing both the sensor interface and MQTT-SN interface allows
Wasm applications to access the on-board sensors and connect with
remote devices. However, as most microcontroller and RTOS do not
provide a substantial access control scheme to restrict the applica-
tion behavior, we introduce a WKD-IBE based encryption scheme
and an access control over MQTT-SN. The benefits of wildcard-
based encryption are fairly straightforward: pattern delegations
can be chained and grouped, thus naturally lending itself to the
many-to-many messaging model of MQTT-SN.
