2.3.2.1 800 MHz Fixed Channel List Definition 499 
The 800 MHz fixed channel list defines 40 channels that may be created. Channel-ID 0 is 500 
863.1 MHz; channels increase at 200 kHz spacing to Channel-ID 34 at 869.9 MHz. Five 501 
additional channels, identified as 35 to 39 , are defined at 865.0625 MHz, 865.4025 MHz, 502 
865.6025 MHz, 865.785 MHz, and 865.985 MHz respectively. ChMask3, ChMask4 , and 503 
ChMask5 are RFU. 504 
 505 
The end -device SHALL create an additional channel at the frequency specified by the 506 
Channel-ID, numbered sequentially in order of Channel-ID, starting after the last default 507 
channel, for each bit set in the CFList. 508 
 509 
These channel definitions represent a  superset of common channels in widespread use in 510 
EU868, IN865, and RU864. 511 
Example: If an end-device uses channel plan EU868, supports CFList  512 
Type 1, and receives it equal to 0x0100_A010_0000_0000_0000_0000, 513 
then ChMaskGrp0 = 0x0100 and ChMaskGrp1=0xA010. Four bits are 514 
set, which correspond to valid channels, so the end-device will create 515 
four channels. EU868 has three default channels, so the first cr eated 516 
channel will be for ChIndex=3. The end-device will create ChIndex=3 517 
at center frequency 863.1MHz, ChIndex=4 at center frequency 518 
863.1+21*0.2 = 867.3MHz, ChIndex=5 at center frequency 519 
863.1+23*0.2 = 867.7MHz, and ChIndex=6 at center frequency 520 
863.1+28*0.2 = 868.7MHz.  521 
Note: The frequencies of the three EU868 default channels correspond 522 
to ChMaskGrp1 = 0x000E. Setting these bits would create new 523 
channels at the same frequency as default channels.  524 
The center frequencies of the four RFID channels under ETSI EN 302 525 
208 correspond to ChMaskGrp0 = 0x0020, ChMaskGrp1 = 0x4900. 526 
Setting these bits would create channels with a higher risk of 527 
interference. 528 
2.3.2.2 900 MHz Fixed Channel List Definition 529 
The 900 MHz fixed channel list defines 96 channels. Channel-ID 0 is 915.1 MHz; channels 530 
increase at 100 kHz intervals to Channel-ID 95 at 924.6 MHz. 531 
