Frequency-Hopping, Spre ad-Spectrum (FHSS) mode, which requires 669 
the device to transmit at a measured conducted power level no greater 670 
than +30 dBm, for a period of no more than 400 msec, and over at least 671 
50 channels, each of which occupy no greater than 250 kHz of 672 
bandwidth and separated by a minimum of 25  kHz or the 20 dB 673 
bandwidth of the hopping channel, whichever is greater. 674 
Digital Transmission System (DTS) mode, which requires that the 675 
device use channels greater than or equal to 500 kHz and comply to a 676 
conducted Power Spect ral Density measurement of no more than +8 677 
dBm per 3 kHz of spectrum.  In practice, this limits the conducted output 678 
power of an end-device to +26 dBm. 679 
Hybrid mode, which requires that the device transmit over multiple 680 
channels (this may be less than the 5 0 channels required for FHSS 681 
mode but is recommended to be at least 4) while complying with the 682 
Power Spectral Density requirements of DTS mode and the 400 msec 683 
dwell time of FHSS mode. In practice , this limits the measured 684 
conducted power of the end-device to 21 dBm. 685 
