Figure 2: AU915-928 channel frequencies 949 
AU915-928 band end-devices MAY use a maximum EIRP of +30 dBm.  950 
AU915-928 end-devices SHALL be capable of operating in the 915 to 928 MHz frequency 951 
band and SHALL feature a channel data structure to store the parameters of 72 channels. A 952 
channel data structure corresponds to a frequency and a set of data rates usable on this 953 
frequency. 954 
If using the over -the-air activation procedure, the end -device SHALL broadcast the Join -955 
Request message alternatively on a random 125 kHz channel amongst the 64 channels  956 
defined using DR2 and on a 500 kHz channel amongst the 8 channels defined using DR6. The 957 
end-device SHOULD change channel for every transmission. 958 
For rapid network acquisition in mixed gateway channel plan environments, the device 959 
SHOULD follow a random channel selection sequence that efficiently probes the octet groups 960 
of eight 125 kHz channels followed by probing one 500 kHz channel each pass.  961 
Each consecutive pass SHOULD NOT select a channel that was used in a previous pass, 962 
until a Join-Request is transmitted on every channel, after which the entire process can restart.  963 
