4 Physical Layer 1796 
 1797 
The LoRaWAN uses a physical layer to communicate with other devices. Three physical 1798 
layers are currently supported through the long range ( LoRa), Long-Range Frequency 1799 
Hopping Spread Spectrum (LR-FHSS), and Frequency shift keying (FSK) modulations. 1800 
4.1 LoRa Description 1801 
4.1.1 LoRa Packet Physical Structure 1802 
LoRa messages use the radio packet explicit header mode, in which the LoRa physical header 1803 
(PHDR) plus a header CRC ( PHDR_CRC) are included. 36 In explicit header mode , the PHDR 1804 
specifies the payload length in bytes, the forward error correction rate, and the presence of an 1805 
OPTIONAL CRC for the payload. The integrity of the payload is protected by a CRC for uplink 1806 
messages. LoRaWAN beacons are tr ansmitted using LoRa  modulation in implicit header 1807 
mode with no payload CRC. The size of the payload depends on the beacon’s data rate . In 1808 
implicit header mode, neither the PHDR nor PHDR_CRC are present. 1809 
The PHDR , PHDR_CRC and payload CRC fields are inserted by the radio transceiver. 1810 
