The LDRO parameter stands for Low Data Rate Optimizer. If set, the modulation alphabet is 1818 
reduced to allow better synchronization and tracking on the receiver. Since such 1819 
synchronization is more difficult on low data rates, it is enabled only on the lowest data rates. 1820 
It also increases the tolerance for multipath delays from simultaneous transmissions (that gain 1821 
does not depend on data rate). This parameter is not signaled in the PHDR. Therefore, it needs 1822 
to be set to a constant value for each data rate. 1823 
