4.1.3 Class B Beacon Frame Content 1827 
The beacon payload BCNPayload consists of a network common part and an OPTIONAL 1828 
gateway-specific part. The size of the RFU fields for each part depend on the LoRa spreading 1829 
factor used to send the beacon. The length is adjusted to fit LoRa modulation interleaving 1830 
blocks, so that the network common part and gateway -specific part are carried by different 1831 
portions of the radio packet. In addition, each part has an independent CRC. As a result, it is 1832 
possible to receive correctly an d detect the correct reception of the network common part, 1833 
even if several gateways transmit concurrently a beacon with different gateway-specific parts. 1834 
In that situation, the gateway-specific part will likely not be received correctly, and this will be 1835 
detected by the CRC.    1836 
