4.3 LR-FHSS Description 1871 
LR-FHSS modulation is only used on the uplink. 1872 
4.3.1 LR-FHSS Physical Layer Description 1873 
LR-FHSS is a fast frequency hopping spread spectrum  (FHSS) modulation with bit rates 1874 
ranging from 162bits/s to 325bits/s. 1875 
When a device transmits a packet using LR-FHSS on a given channel, the packet content is 1876 
modulated across several pseudo-random frequencies that spans the interval: 1877 
𝐹𝑖𝑛𝑡𝑒𝑟𝑣𝑎𝑙 = 𝑐𝑒𝑛𝑡𝑟𝑒𝑓𝑟𝑒𝑞 ±    𝑏𝑤/2 1878 
For FCC 47 CFR Part 15 compliance, the end -device frequency hops across 60 physical 1879 
channels on a 25.4 kHz frequency grid. 1880 
For ETSI based countries, the end-device frequency hops across 35 or 86 physical channels 1881 
on a 3.9 kHz frequency grid. 1882 
All physical channels are statistically used equally. 1883 
The transmission starts on a random frequency inside the interval, and the following frequency 1884 
hopping pattern is also randomly selected and announced in the LR-FHSS packet physical 1885 
header. The transmission carrier frequency changes every 102.4 m sec for each payload 1886 
fragment, and 233.472 msec for each PHY header. 1887 
The instantaneous LR-FHSS modulation bandwidth is 488 Hz. Therefore, a single LR-FHSS 1888 
channel actually corresponds to many physical frequency channels.  1889 
The LR-FHSS frequency hopping bandwidth is region-specific. 1890 
