 Bi-directional end-devices with maximal receive slots (Class C): Class C-capable end-352 
devices allow nearly continuously open receive windows , which are closed only when 353 
transmitting. Class C-enabled end-devices use more power to operate than Class A or Class 354 
B-enabled, but they feature the lowest latency for communication between servers and end-355 
devices. 356

