6.2.6 Join-Accept frame 1457 
The Network SHALL respond to a Join-Request frame with a Join-Accept frame if the end-1458 
device is permitted to join the network.  The Join-Accept frame is sent like a normal downlink 1459 
but uses delays JOIN_ACCEPT_DELAY1 or JOIN_ACCEPT_DELAY2 (instead of 1460 
RECEIVE_DELAY1 and RECEIVE_DELAY2, respectively). The channel frequency and data 1461 
rate used for these two receive windows are identical to the ones used for the RX1 and RX2 1462 
receive windows described in Section 3.3 and SHALL use the default values defined in the  1463 
Regional Parameters [RP002] specification. 1464 
A Join-Accept response SHALL NOT be given to the end-device if the Join-Request is not 1465 
accepted. 1466 
                                                
