10.3 Minimizing Timing Drift 1818 
The end-devices MAY use the beacon’s precise periodicity (when available) to calibrate their 1819 
internal clock and therefore reduce the initial clock frequency imprecision. As the timing 1820 
oscillators exhibit a predictable temperature frequency shift, the use of a temperature sensor 1821 
could enable further minimization of the timing drift. 1822

