16.4 Downlink Timing for Frame-Pending Frames 2480 
The following diagram illustrates the use of the FPending bit on a downlink. The FPending 2481 
bit can only be set on a downlink frame. When present in a downlink received in a Class A 2482 
receive window, the FPending bit informs the end-device that the Network has one or more 2483 
downlink frames pending for the end-device. When present in a downlink received in a Class 2484 
B ping-slot, FPending is used to prioritize conflicting ping slots, see Section 9.2 for details. 2485 
FPending has no meaning in a downlink received in a Class C RXC window. 2486

