UEFI (Unified Extensible 
Firmware Interface) 
One form of Host Processor Boot Firmware which uses a Unified 
Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) structure (as defined by the 
UEFI Forum). 
UEFI Drivers 
 
Standalone binary executables which are loaded during the boot 
process to handle specific pieces of hardware. 
Unambiguous Physical 
Presence 
Indicates authorization by a local person that cannot be impersonated 
