3.4.3.2 Image Data Access Across the Enterprise 
Scenario Two, as shown in Figure 3-3, examines multiple departments that use disparate imaging 
devices for acquisition and may involve multiple PACS [13]. The assumption is that different 
departments have separate clinical staff and different medical imaging goals and may use different 
means to centralize their medical images. This scenario simulates a hospital, in that radiology is not the 
only department that uses medical imaging, nor does the radiology department mandate use of its PACS 
to centralize medical images across a hospital. Aggregation and centralized management remain the 
goal, but the practice guide describes other components in the ecosystem that enable broader clinical 
functionality. While PACS implements central medical image storage, access to images is not permitted 
for all clinical staff. 
