Framework to Federal Information Systems—material that is available to the public [12]. The risk 
management framework (RMF) guidance, as a whole, proved to be invaluable in giving us a baseline to 
assess risks, from which we developed the project, the security characteristics of the build, and this 
guide. 
It is important to understand what constitutes the definition of risk, as it relates to non-traditional 
information systems, such as wireless infusion pumps. NIST SP 800-37 presents three tiers in the risk 
management hierarchy (Figure 4-1): 
▪ Tier 1: Organization 
▪ Tier 2: Mission/Business Process 
▪ Tier 3: Information System 
