A guest network allows visitors or patients to access internet services during their visit. As explained in 
Section 5.3.1.1.2, the work traffic tends not to be of a clinical nature, but is offered as a courtesy to 
hospital visitors and patients to access the internet. The external firewall marks the boundary between

