7.3 Security Analysis Summary 
Our reference design’s implementation of security surrounding wireless infusion pumps helps reduce 
risk from a pump, even if a vulnerability is identified in a pump, by creating a more secure environment 
for medical devices. The key feature is network segmentation. Supporting this zone approach, our 
project build follows security best practices to harden devices, monitor traffic, and limit access via the 
wireless network to only authorized users. Any organization following this guide must conduct its own 
analysis of how to employ the elements, in their own environment, that were discussed here. It is 
essential that organizations follow security best practices to address potential vulnerabilities and to 
minimize any risk to the operational network. 
