2.1.7.3 Wireless AP Connection and Setup 
Connect the APs to the Ethernet ports configured for untagged VLAN 1520. The APs will automatically 
obtain their addresses and the WLC address via DHCP from the switch (see Section 2.1.6). No other 
VLANs should to be configured for the APs because we are using a centralized switching model where 
Wi-Fi traffic VLANs are connected to the enterprise network through the WLC. 
As each AP is connected, it should show up in the Wireless tab on the WLC. For each AP, the AP Mode 
needs to be set to FlexConnect, as shown below. 
 
2.1.7.4 Authentication Configuration 
To use certificate-based authentication, the WLC must consult a remote authentication dial-in user 
service (RADIUS) server. Configure the Cisco Identity Services Engine (ISE) RADIUS server IP address and 
shared secret at Security > RADIUS > Authentication > New.

