3.3.4 PUBLISH Actions 1715 
The receiver of a PUBLISH Packet MUST respond with the packet as determined by the QoS in the 1716 
PUBLISH Packet [MQTT-3.3.4-1]. 1717 
 1718 
Table 3-3 Expected PUBLISH packet response 1719 
QoS Level Expected Response 
QoS 0 None 
QoS 1 PUBACK packet 
QoS 2 PUBREC packet 
 1720 
The Client uses a PUBLISH packet to send an Application Message to the Server, for distribution to 1721 
Clients with matching subscriptions. 1722 
 1723 
The Server uses a PUBLISH packet to send an Application Message to each Client which has a matching 1724 
subscription. The PUBLISH packet includes the Subscription Identifier carried in the SUBSCRIBE packet, 1725 
if there was one. 1726 
 1727 
When Clients make subscriptions with Topic Filters that include wildcards, it is possible for a Client’s 1728 
subscriptions to overlap so that a published message might match multiple filters. In this case the Server 1729 
MUST deliver the message to the Client respecting the maximum QoS of all the matching subscriptions 1730 
[MQTT-3.3.4-2]. In addition, the Server MAY deliver further copies of the message, one for each 1731 
additional matching subscription and respecting the subscription’s QoS in each case.  1732 
