The Session State in the Server consists of: 2703 
• The existence of a Session, even if the rest of the Session State is empty. 2704 
• The Clients subscriptions, including any Subscription Identifiers. 2705 
• QoS 1 and QoS 2 messages which have been sent to the Client, but have not been completely 2706 
acknowledged. 2707 
• QoS 1 and QoS 2 messages pending transmission to the Client and OPTIONALLY QoS 0 messages 2708 
pending transmission to the Client. 2709 
• QoS 2 messages which have been received from the Client, but have not been completely 2710 
acknowledged.The Will Message and the Will Delay Interval 2711 
• If the Session is currently not connected, the time at which the Session will end and Session State will 2712 
be discarded. 2713 
