Non-normative comment 2919 
The rules listed above ensure that when a stream of messages is published and subscribed to an 2920 
Ordered Topic with QoS 1, the final copy of each message received by the subscribers will be in 2921 
the order that they were published. If the message is re-sent the duplicate message can be 2922 
received after one of the earlier messages is received. For example, a publisher might send 2923 
messages in the order 1,2,3,4 but the subscriber might receive them in the order 1,2,3,2,3,4 if 2924 
there is a network disconnection after message 3 has been sent. 2925 
