• AMQP v1.0 Final, 07 October 2011. http://www.amqp.org/speciﬁcation/1.0/amqp-org-download
Abstract:
The Advanced Message Queuing Protocol (AMQP) is an open internet protocol for business messaging. It deﬁnes a binary
wire-level protocol that allows for the reliable exchange of business messages between two parties. AMQP has a layered
architecture and the speciﬁcation is organized as a set of parts that reﬂects that architecture. Part 1 deﬁnes the AMQP type
system and encoding. Part 2 deﬁnes the AMQP transport layer, an efﬁcient, binary, peer-to-peer protocol for transporting
messages between two processes over a network. Part 3 deﬁnes the AMQP message format, with a concrete encoding. Part
4 deﬁnes how interactions can be grouped within atomic transactions. Part 5 deﬁnes the AMQP security layers.
