PART 2. TRANSPORT 2.3 Framing
• If the server cannot parse the protocol header, the server MUST send a valid protocol header with a sup-
ported protocol version and then close the socket.
• Note that if the server only supports a single protocol version, it is consistent with the above rules for the
server to send its protocol header prior to receiving anything from the client and to subsequently close the
socket if the client’s protocol header does not match the server’s.
Based on this behavior a client can discover which protocol versions a server supports by attempting to connect
with its highest supported version and reconnecting with a version less than or equal to the version received back
from the server.
TCP Client TCP Server
