PART 2. TRANSPORT 2.4 Connections
2.4.2 Pipelined Open
For applications that use many short-lived connections, it MAY be desirable to pipeline the connection negotiation
process. A peer MAY do this by starting to send subsequent frames before receiving the partner’s connection
header or open frame. This is permitted so long as the pipelined frames are known a priori to conform to the
capabilities and limitations of its partner. For example, this can be accomplished by keeping the use of the
connection within the capabilities and limits expected of all AMQP implementations as deﬁned by the speciﬁcation
of the open frame.
