The ﬂow control semantics deﬁned in this section provide the primitives necessary to implement a wide variety of
ﬂow control strategies. Additionally, by manipulating the link-credit and drain ﬂag, a receiver can provide a variety
of different higher level behaviors often useful to applications, including synchronous blocking fetch, synchronous
fetch with a timeout, asynchronous notiﬁcations, and stopping/pausing.
