3. LPWAN Architecture 
LPWAN architectures are similar among them, but each LPWAN technology names architecture
elements diﬀerently. In this document, we use terminology from , which identiﬁes the
following entities in a typical LPWAN (see Figure 1):
Devices (Dev) are the end-devices or hosts (e.g., sensors, actuators, etc.). There can be a very
high density of devices per Radio Gateway. 
The Radio Gateway (RGW) is the endpoint of the constrained link. 
The Network Gateway (NGW) is the interconnection node between the Radio Gateway and
the Internet. 
The Application Server (App) is the endpoint of the application-level protocol on the Internet
side. 
