7.4.1. Processing Fixed-Length Fields 
If the ﬁeld is identiﬁed in the Field Descriptor as being of ﬁxed length, then applying the CDA to
compress this ﬁeld results in a ﬁxed amount of bits. The residue for that ﬁeld is simply the bits
resulting from applying the CDA to the ﬁeld. This value may be empty (e.g., not-sent CDA), in
which case the ﬁeld residue is absent from the Compression Residue.
