7.4.3. Not-Sent CDA 
The not-sent action can be used when the ﬁeld value is speciﬁed in a Rule and, therefore, known
by both the Compressor and the Decompressor. This action  be used with the ""equal"" MO.
If MO is ""ignore"", there is a risk of having a decompressed ﬁeld value that is diﬀerent from the
original ﬁeld that was compressed.
The compressor does not send any residue for a ﬁeld on which not-sent compression is applied.
The decompressor restores the ﬁeld value with the TV stored in the matched Rule identiﬁed by
the received RuleID.
