8.4.1.1. Sender Behavior 
At the beginning of the fragmentation of a new SCHC Packet, the fragment sender  select a
RuleID and DTag value pair for this SCHC Packet.
Each SCHC Fragment  contain exactly one tile in its Payload. The tile  be at least the
size of an L2 Word. The sender  transmit the SCHC Fragments messages in the order that
the tiles appear in the SCHC Packet. Except for the last tile of a SCHC Packet, each tile  be of
a size that complements the SCHC Fragment Header so that the SCHC Fragment is a multiple of
L2 Words without the need for padding bits. Except for the last one, the SCHC Fragments 
use the Regular SCHC Fragment format speciﬁed in Section 8.3.1.1. The SCHC Fragment that
carries the last tile  be an All-1 SCHC Fragment, described in Section 8.3.1.2.
The sender  transmit a SCHC Sender-Abort.
