Then, upon receiving a SCHC ACK:
if the SCHC ACK indicates that some tiles are missing at the receiver, then the sender 
transmit all the tiles that have been reported missing, it  increment Attempts, it 
reset the Retransmission Timer, and  await the next SCHC ACK. 
if the current window is not the last one and the SCHC ACK indicates that all tiles were
correctly received, the sender  stop the Retransmission Timer, it  advance to the
next fragmentation window, and it  start a blind transmission phase as described
above. 
if the current window is the last one and the SCHC ACK indicates that more tiles were
received than the sender sent, the fragment sender  send a SCHC Sender-Abort, and it
