10. SCHC Compression for IPv6 and UDP Headers 
This section lists the IPv6 and UDP header ﬁelds and describes how they can be compressed. An
example of a set of Rules for UDP/IPv6 header compression is provided in Appendix A.
10.1. IPv6 Version Field 
The IPv6 version ﬁeld is labeled by the protocol parser as being the ""version"" ﬁeld of the IPv6
protocol. Therefore, it only exists for IPv6 packets. In the Rule, TV is set to 6, MO to ""ignore"" and
CDA to ""not-sent"".
10.2. IPv6 Traﬃc Class Field 
If the Diﬀserv ﬁeld does not vary and is known by both sides, the Field Descriptor in the Rule 
