Figures 26 to 28 describe an example of a Rule set.
In this example, 0 was chosen as the special RuleID that tags packets that cannot be compressed
with any compression Rule.
All the ﬁelds described in Rules 1-3 are present in the IPv6 and UDP headers. The DevIID value is
inferred from the L2 header.
Rules 2-3 use global addresses. The way the Dev learns the preﬁx is not in the scope of the
document.
Rule 3 compresses each port number to 4 bits.
