Appendix D. SCHC Parameters 
This section lists the information that needs to be provided in the LPWAN technology-speciﬁc
documents.
Most common uses cases, deployment scenarios. 
Mapping of the SCHC architectural elements onto the LPWAN architecture. 
Assessment of LPWAN integrity checking. 
Various potential channel conditions for the technology and the corresponding
recommended use of SCHC C/D and SCHC F/R. 
This section lists the parameters that need to be deﬁned in the Proﬁle.
RuleID numbering scheme, ﬁxed-size or variable-size RuleIDs, number of Rules, the way the
RuleID is transmitted. 
maximum packet size that should ever be reconstructed by SCHC decompression
(MAX_PACKET_SIZE). See Section 12. 
Padding: size of the L2 Word (for most LPWAN technologies, this would be a byte; for some
technologies, a bit). 
Decision to use SCHC fragmentation mechanism or not. If yes, the document must describe:
reliability mode(s) used, in which cases (e.g., based on link channel condition). 
RuleID values assigned to each mode in use. 
presence and number of bits for DTag (T) for each RuleID value, lifetime of DTag at the
receiver. 
support for interleaved packet transmission, to what extent. 
