5. SDP ""sctp-port"" Attribute 
5.1. General 
This section deﬁnes a new SDP media-level attribute, ""sctp-port"". The attribute can be associated
with an SDP media description (""m="" line) with a ""UDP/DTLS/SCTP"" or a ""TCP/DTLS/SCTP"" proto
value. In that case, the ""m="" line port value indicates the port of the underlying transport-layer
protocol (UDP or TCP), and the ""sctp-port"" value indicates the SCTP port.
