9. Association and Connection Management 
9.1. General 
This section describes how to manage an SCTP association, DTLS association, and TCP connection
using SDP attributes.
The SCTP association, the DTLS association, and the TCP connection are managed independently
from each other. Each can be established and closed without impacting others.
The detailed SDP oﬀer/answer  procedures for the SDP attributes are described in 
Section 10.
[RFC3264]
9.2. SDP ""sendrecv""/""sendonly""/""recvonly""/""inactive"" Attributes 
This speciﬁcation does not deﬁne semantics for the SDP direction attributes . Unless
the semantics of these attributes for an SCTP association usage have been deﬁned, SDP direction
attributes  be ignored if present.
[RFC4566]
