9.3. SCTP Association 
When an SCTP association is established, both SCTP endpoints  initiate the SCTP association
(i.e., both SCTP endpoints take the ""active"" role). In addition, both endpoints  use the same
SCTP port as client port and server port, in order to prevent two separate SCTP associations from
being established.
As both SCTP endpoints take the ""active"" role, the SDP ""setup"" attribute  does not apply
to SCTP association establishment. However, the ""setup"" attribute does apply to establishment of
the underlying DTLS association and TCP connection.
