Encrypted Key Transport for DTLS and Secure RTP
Abstract
Encrypted Key Transport (EKT) is an extension to DTLS (Datagram Transport Layer Security) and
the Secure Real-time Transport Protocol (SRTP) that provides for the secure transport of SRTP
master keys, rollover counters, and other information within SRTP. This facility enables SRTP for
decentralized conferences by distributing a common key to all of the conference endpoints.
