These ﬁelds and data elements are deﬁned as follows:
EKTPlaintext:
This is the data that is input to the EKT encryption operation. This data never appears on the
wire; it is used only in computations internal to EKT. This is the concatenation of the SRTP
master key and its length, the SSRC, and the ROC. 
EKTCiphertext:
This is the data that is output from the EKT encryption operation (see Section 4.4). This ﬁeld is
included in SRTP packets when EKT is in use. The length of the EKTCiphertext can be larger
than the length of the EKTPlaintext that was encrypted. 
SRTPMasterKey:
On the sender side, this is the SRTP master key associated with the indicated SSRC. 
SRTPMasterKeyLength:
This is the length of the SRTPMasterKey in bytes. This depends on the cipher suite negotiated
for SRTP using Session Description Protocol (SDP) Oﬀer/Answer . 
