4.4.1. AES Key Wrap 
The default EKT Cipher is the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) Key Wrap with Padding
algorithm . It requires a plaintext length M that is at least one octet, and it returns a
ciphertext with a length of N = M + (M mod 8) + 8 octets. It can be used with key sizes of L = 16
octets or L = 32 octets, and its use with those key sizes is indicated as AESKW128 or AESKW256,
respectively. The key size determines the length of the AES key used by the Key Wrap algorithm.
With this cipher, T=248.
