In some systems, when a member of a conference leaves the conference, that conference is
rekeyed so that the member who left the conference no longer has the key. When changing to a
new EKTKey, it is possible that the attacker could block the EKTKey message getting to a
particular endpoint and that endpoint would keep sending media encrypted using the old key. To
mitigate that risk, the lifetime of the EKTKey  be limited by using the ekt_ttl.MUST
