2.2. Discovering Support 
Extended token lengths require support from server implementations. Support can be
discovered by a client implementation in one of two ways:
Where Capabilities and Settings Messages (CSMs) are available, such as in CoAP over TCP,
support can be discovered using the Extended-Token-Length Capability Option deﬁned in 
Section 2.2.1. 
Otherwise, such as in CoAP over UDP, support can only be discovered by trial and error, as
described in Section 2.2.2. 
