TCP Usage Guidance in the Internet of Things (IoT)
Abstract
This document provides guidance on how to implement and use the Transmission Control
Protocol (TCP) in Constrained-Node Networks (CNNs), which are a characteristic of the Internet
of Things (IoT). Such environments require a lightweight TCP implementation and may not make
use of optional functionality. This document explains a number of known and deployed
techniques to simplify a TCP stack as well as corresponding trade-oﬀs. The objective is to help
embedded developers with decisions on which TCP features to use.
