6. Enhancements to RFC 6550 
This document speciﬁes a new behavior whereby a 6LR injects DAO messages for unicast
addresses (see Section 9) and multicast addresses (see Section 10) on behalf of leaves that are not
aware of RPL. The RUL addresses are exposed as external targets . Conforming to 
, IPv6-in-IPv6 encapsulation between the 6LR and the RPL DODAG root is used to carry
the RPL artifacts and remove them when forwarding outside the RPL domain, e.g., to a RUL.
This document also synchronizes the liveness monitoring at the root and the 6LBR. The same
lifetime value is used for both, and a single keep-alive message, the RPL DAO, traverses the RPL
network. Another new behavior is introduced whereby the RPL DODAG root proxies the EDAR
message to the 6LBR on behalf of the 6LR (see Section 8), for any leaf node that implements the
6LN functionality described in .
 introduces the RPL Target option, which can be used in RPL control
