of 0. It is up to the registering 6LN to maintain the corresponding route from then on, by either
(1) keeping it active via a diﬀerent 6LR or (2) acting as a RAN and managing its own reachability.
When forwarding a packet from the RUL into the RPL domain, if the packet does not have an RPI,
the 6LR  encapsulate the packet to the root and add an RPI. If there is an RPI in the packet,
the 6LR  rewrite the RPI, but it does not need to encapsulate.
