1. Introduction 
The SCHC speciﬁcation  describes generic header compression and fragmentation
techniques that can be used on all Low-Power Wide Area Network (LPWAN) technologies deﬁned
in . Even though those technologies share a great number of common features like
star-oriented topologies, network architecture, devices with communications that are mostly
quite predictable, etc., they do have some slight diﬀerences with respect to payload sizes,
reactiveness, etc.
SCHC provides a generic framework that enables those devices to communicate on IP networks.
However, for eﬃcient performance, some parameters and modes of operation need to be set
appropriately for each of the LPWAN technologies.
This document describes the parameters and modes of operation when SCHC is used over
LoRaWAN networks. The LoRaWAN protocol is speciﬁed by the LoRa Alliance in 
.
