5. SCHC over LoRaWAN
5.1. LoRaWAN FPort and RuleID 
The FPort ﬁeld is part of the SCHC Message, as shown in Figure 5. The SCHC C/D and the SCHC F/R
 concatenate the FPort ﬁeld with the LoRaWAN payload to recompose the SCHC Message.SHALL
RFC 9011 SCHC over LoRaWAN April 2021
Gimenez & Petrov Standards Track Page 9

Note: The SCHC Message is any datagram sent by the SCHC C/D or F/R layers.
A fragmented datagram with application payload transferred from device to Network Gateway is
called an ""uplink-fragmented datagram"". It uses an FPort for data uplink and its associated SCHC
control downlinks, named ""FPortUp"" in this document. The other way, a fragmented datagram
with application payload transferred from Network Gateway to device is called a ""downlink-
fragmented datagram"". It uses another FPort for data downlink and its associated SCHC control
uplinks, named ""FPortDown"" in this document.
All RuleIDs can use arbitrary values inside the FPort range allowed by the LoRaWAN
speciﬁcation  and  be shared by the device and SCHC gateway prior to the
communication with the selected rule. The uplink and downlink fragmentation FPorts  be
diﬀerent.
