4.2. CNSA TLS Authentication 
For server and/or client authentication, CNSA (D)TLS  generate and verify either ECDSA
signatures or RSA signatures.
In all cases, the client  authenticate the server. The server  also authenticate the client,
as needed by the speciﬁc application.
The public keys used to verify these signatures  be contained in a certiﬁcate (see Section 5.4
for more information).
