B.4. A Note on Diﬀerences between Link-Format and Link Header Fields 
While link-format and Link header ﬁelds look very similar and are based on the same model of
typed links, there are some diﬀerences between  and . When implementing an
RD or interacting with an RD, care must be taken to follow the behavior described in 
whenever application/link-format  representations are used.
""Default value of anchor"": Under both  and , relative references in the
term inside the angle brackets (the target) and the anchor attribute are resolved against the
relevant base URI (which usually is the URI used to retrieve the entity) and independent of
each other.
When, in a Link header , the anchor attribute is absent, the link's context is the URI
of the selected representation (and usually equal to the base URI).
