In links per , if the anchor attribute is absent, the default value is the Origin of (for
all relevant cases, the URI reference / resolved against) the link's target.
There is no percent encoding in link-format documents.
A link-format document is a UTF-8-encoded string of Unicode characters and does not have
percent encoding, while Link header ﬁelds are practically ASCII strings that use percent
encoding for non-ASCII characters, stating the encoding explicitly when required.
For example, while a Link header ﬁeld in a page about a Swedish city might read:
a link-format document from the same source might describe the link as:
