11. Security Considerations 
Security considerations discussed in  should be taken into account.
Security considerations discussed in Sections 11.3 and 11.4 of  should also be taken into
account.
OSCORE provides end-to-end protection of all information that is not required for proxy
operations and requires that a security context is set up ( ). It can be
trusted that the source endpoint is legitimate even if the NoSec mode is used. However, an
intermediary node can modify the unprotected Outer Q-Block1 and/or Q-Block2 options to cause
a Q-Block transfer to fail or keep requesting all the blocks by setting the M bit and thus causing
attack ampliﬁcation. As discussed in , applications need to consider that
certain message ﬁelds and message types are not protected end to end and may be spoofed or
manipulated. Therefore, it is  to use the NoSec mode if either the Q-Block1 or
Q-Block2 option is used.
