5.2. Tunnel Establishment Procedures 
Either the Media Distributor or Key Distributor initiates the establishment of a TLS tunnel. Which
entity acts as the TLS client when establishing the tunnel and what event triggers the
establishment of the tunnel are outside the scope of this document. Further, how the trust
relationships are established between the Key Distributor and Media Distributor are also outside
the scope of this document.
A tunnel  be a mutually authenticated TLS connection.
The Media Distributor or Key Distributor  establish a tunnel prior to forwarding tunneled
DTLS messages. Given the time-sensitive nature of DTLS-SRTP procedures, a tunnel  be
established prior to the Media Distributor receiving a DTLS message from an endpoint.
A single tunnel  be used to relay DTLS messages between any number of endpoints and the
Key Distributor.
A Media Distributor  have more than one tunnel established between itself and one or more
Key Distributors. When multiple tunnels are established, which tunnel or tunnels to use to send
messages for a given conference is outside the scope of this document.
