The specification in this document is called the ""framework"" or ""ACE framework"". When
referring to ""profiles of this framework"", it refers to additional specifications that define the use
of this specification with concrete transport and communication security protocols (e.g., CoAP
over DTLS).
The term ""Access Information"" is used for parameters, other than the access token, provided to
the client by the AS to enable it to access the RS (e.g., public key of the RS or profile supported by
RS).
The term ""authorization information"" is used to denote all information, including the claims of
relevant access tokens, that an RS uses to determine whether an access request should be
granted.
