3. Overview 
This specification defines the ACE framework for authorization in the Internet of Things
environment. It consists of a set of building blocks.
The basic block is the OAuth 2.0  framework, which enjoys widespread deployment.
Many IoT devices can support OAuth 2.0 without any additional extensions, but for certain
constrained settings, additional profiling is needed.
Another building block is the lightweight web transfer protocol CoAP , for those
communication environments where HTTP is not appropriate. CoAP typically runs on top of UDP,
which further reduces overhead and message exchanges. While this specification defines
extensions for the use of OAuth over CoAP, other underlying protocols are not prohibited from
being supported in the future, such as HTTP/2 , Message Queuing Telemetry Transport
(MQTT) , Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) , and QUIC . Note that this
