5.1. Discovering Authorization Servers 
The C must discover the AS in charge of the RS to determine where to request the access token.
To do so, the C 1) must find out the AS URI to which the token request message must be sent and
2)  validate that the AS with this URI is authorized to provide access tokens for this RS.
In order to determine the AS URI, the C  send an initial Unauthorized Resource Request
message to the RS. The RS then denies the request and sends the address of its AS back to the C
(see Section 5.2). How the C validates the AS authorization is not in scope for this document. The
C may, for example, ask its owner if this AS is authorized for this RS. The C may also use a
mechanism that addresses both problems at once (e.g., by querying a dedicated secure service
provided by the client owner) .
