In the example above, the response parameter AS points the receiver of this message to the URI
""coaps://as.example.com/token"" to request access tokens. The RS sending this response uses an
internal clock that is not synchronized with the clock of the AS. Therefore, it cannot reliably
verify the expiration time of access tokens it receives. Nevertheless, to ensure a certain level of
access token freshness, the RS has included a cnonce parameter (see Section 5.3.1) in the
response. (The hex sequence of the cnonce parameter is encoded in CBOR-based notation in this
example.)
