5.6. AS Authentication 
The client credentials grant does not, by default, authenticate the AS that the client connects to.
In classic OAuth, the AS is authenticated with a TLS server certificate.
Profiles of this framework  specify how clients authenticate the AS and how
communication security is implemented. By default, server side TLS certificates, as defined by
OAuth 2.0, are required.
