5.7. The Authorization Endpoint 
The OAuth 2.0 authorization endpoint is used to interact with the resource owner and obtain an
authorization grant in certain grant flows. The primary use case for the ACE-OAuth framework is
for machine-to-machine interactions that do not involve the resource owner in the authorization
flow; therefore, this endpoint is out of scope here. Future profiles may define constrained
adaptation mechanisms for this endpoint as well. Nonconstrained clients interacting with
constrained resource servers can use the specification in  and the attack
countermeasures suggested in .
