Datagram Transport Layer Security (DTLS) Profile
for Authentication and Authorization for
Constrained Environments (ACE)
Abstract
This specification defines a profile of the Authentication and Authorization for Constrained
Environments (ACE) framework that allows constrained servers to delegate client authentication
and authorization. The protocol relies on DTLS version 1.2 or later for communication security
between entities in a constrained network using either raw public keys or pre-shared keys. A
resource-constrained server can use this protocol to delegate management of authorization
information to a trusted host with less-severe limitations regarding processing power and
memory.
