4.10.7. Layer 2 Parameters 
The data model includes two parameters needed for fragmentation:
l2-word-size:  base fragmentation, in bits, on a Layer 2 Word that can be of any
length. The default value is 8 and corresponds to the default value for the byte-aligned Layer
2. A value of 1 will indicate that there is no alignment and no need for padding. 
maximum-packet-size: defines the maximum size of an uncompressed datagram. By default,
the value is set to 1280 bytes. 
They are defined as unsigned integers; see Section 6.
