2.1. Client Token Request to the Authorization Server (AS) 
The first step in the protocol flow (Figure 1, step (A)) is the token acquisition by the Client from
the AS. The Client and the AS  perform mutual authentication. The Client requests an access
token from the AS, as described in . The document
follows the procedures defined in  for raw public keys
(RPKs) ) and in  for pre-shared keys (PSKs). However, the
content type of the request is set to ""application/ace+json"", and the AS uses JSON in the Payload of
its responses to the Client and the RS. As explained earlier, implementations  also use the
""application/ace+cbor"" content type.
On receipt of the token request, the AS verifies the request. If the AS successfully verifies the
access token request and authorizes the Client for the indicated audience (i.e., RS) and scopes
(i.e., publish/subscribe permissions over topics, as described in Section 2.3), the AS issues an
access token (Figure 1, step (B)).
The response includes the parameters described in 
. For RPKs, the parameters are as described in 
. For PSKs, the document follows . In both
cases, if the response contains an ""ace_profile"" parameter, this parameter is set to ""mqtt_tls"". The
returned token is a Proof-of-Possession (PoP) token by default.
