2.4.2. Authorization Success 
On success, the reason code of the CONNACK is 0x00 (Success). If the Broker starts a new Session,
it  also set Session Present to 0 in the CONNACK packet to signal a new Session to the Client.
Otherwise, it  set Session Present to 1.
Having accepted the connection, the Broker  be prepared to store the token during the
connection and after disconnection for future use. If the token is not self-contained and the
Broker uses token introspection, it  cache the validation result to authorize the subsequent
PUBLISH and SUBSCRIBE packets. PUBLISH and SUBSCRIBE packets, which are sent after a
connection setup, do not contain access tokens. If the introspection result is not cached, the
Broker needs to introspect the saved token for each request. The Broker  also use a cache
timeout to introspect tokens regularly. The timeout value is specific to the application and should
be chosen to reduce the risk of using stale introspection responses.
