time. For QoS > 1, the message expiry interval dictates how long the retained message is kept.
However, it is important that the Broker avoids sending messages indefinitely for the Clients that
never update their tokens (i.e., the Client connects briefly with a valid token, sends a PUBLISH
packet with the RETAIN flag set to 1 and QoS > 1, disconnects, and never connects again).
Therefore, the Broker  use the minimum of the token expiry and message expiry interval to
discard a retained message.
In case of disconnections due to network errors or server disconnection due to a protocol error
(which includes authorization errors), the Will Message is sent if the Client supplied a Will in the
CONNECT packet. The Client's token scope array  include the Will Topic. The Will Message 
 be published to the Will Topic, regardless of whether the corresponding token has expired
(as it has been validated and accepted during CONNECT).
