3.1. SCHC Compound ACK Message Format 
Figure 1 shows the success SCHC ACK format, i.e., when all fragments have been correctly
received (C=1), as defined in .
In case SCHC Fragment losses are found in any of the windows of the SCHC Packet, the SCHC
Compound ACK  be used. The SCHC Compound ACK message format is shown in Figures 2
and 3.
[RFC8724]
Figure 1: SCHC Success ACK Message Format, as Defined in RFC 8724 
