3.5.1.4. Two-Byte SCHC Header for Uplink Fragmentation 
ACK-on-Error with a two-byte header  be used for medium- to large-sized packets that need
to be sent reliably. ACK-on-Error is optimal for reliable SCHC Packet transmission over Sigfox,
since it leads to a reduced number of ACKs in the lower-capacity Downlink channel. Also,
Downlink messages can be sent asynchronously and opportunistically. In contrast, ACK-Always
would not minimize the number of ACKs, and No-ACK would not allow reliable transmission.
