5.2. Uplink ACK-on-Error Examples: Single-Byte SCHC Header 
The Single-byte SCHC Header ACK-on-Error mode allows sending up to 28 fragments and packet
sizes up to 300 bytes. The SCHC Fragments may be delivered asynchronously, and Downlink ACK
can be sent opportunistically.
Case No Losses
The Downlink flag must be enabled in the sender Uplink message to allow a Downlink message
from the receiver. The Downlink Enable in the figures shows where the sender  enable the
Downlink and wait for an ACK.
Case Fragment Losses in the First Window
In this case, fragments are lost in the first window (W=0). After the first All-0 message arrives, the
receiver leverages the opportunity and sends a SCHC ACK with the corresponding bitmap and
C=0.
