"rfc_rfc_9556_internet_of_things_iot_edge_challenges_cac07e31.pdf","RFC 9556
Internet of Things (IoT) Edge Challenges and
Functions
Abstract
Many Internet of Things (IoT) applications have requirements that cannot be satisfied by
centralized cloud-based systems (i.e., cloud computing). These include time sensitivity, data
volume, connectivity cost, operation in the face of intermittent services, privacy, and security. As
a result, IoT is driving the Internet toward edge computing. This document outlines the
requirements of the emerging IoT edge and its challenges. It presents a general model and major
components of the IoT edge to provide a common basis for future discussions in the Thing-to-
Thing Research Group (T2TRG) and other IRTF and IETF groups. This document is a product of
the IRTF T2TRG.
