"rfc_rfc_9594_key_provisioning_for_group_communicatio_d725a79f.pdf","RFC 9594
Key Provisioning for Group Communication Using
Authentication and Authorization for Constrained
Environments (ACE)
Abstract
This document defines how to use the Authentication and Authorization for Constrained
Environments (ACE) framework to distribute keying material and configuration parameters for
secure group communication. Candidate group members that act as Clients and are authorized to
join a group can do so by interacting with a Key Distribution Center (KDC) acting as the Resource
Server, from which they obtain the keying material to communicate with other group members.
While defining general message formats as well as the interface and operations available at the
KDC, this document supports different approaches and protocols for secure group
communication. Therefore, details are delegated to separate application profiles of this
document as specialized instances that target a particular group communication approach and
define how communications in the group are protected. Compliance requirements for such
application profiles are also specified.
