4.4. Computing the Token Hash
Once HASH_INPUT is determined as defined in Sections 4.2 and 4.3, a hash value of HASH_INPUT
is generated as per . The resulting output in binary format is used as the
token hash. Note that the used binary format embeds the identifier of the used hash function in
the first byte of the computed token hash.
The specific hash function used  be collision resistant on byte strings and  be selected
from the ""Named Information Hash Algorithm Registry"" . Consistent
with the compliance requirements in , the hash function sha-256 as
specified in  is mandatory to implement.
The AS specifies the used hash function to registered devices during their registration procedure
(see Section 10).
