C.3. Full Query with Observe and Diff Query
Figure 12 shows an interaction example of a CoAP observation and a full query of the TRL.
The example also shows one of the notifications from the AS getting lost in transmission; thus,
that notification does not reach the RS.
When this happens, and after a waiting time defined by the application has elapsed, the RS
sends a GET request with no Observe Option to the AS, asking the AS to perform a diff query of
the TRL. The RS indicates N = 8 as the value of the 'diff' query parameter, i.e., as the maximum
number of diff entries to be included in a response from the AS.
In this example, the AS does not support the ""Cursor"" extension. Hence, the 'cursor' parameter is
not included in the payload of the responses to a full query request. Also, the 'cursor' parameter
and the 'more' parameter are not included in the payload of the responses to a diff query request.
