5. TLS Cipher Suites Registry
Several categories of cipher suites are discouraged for general use and are marked as ""D"".
Cipher suites that use NULL encryption do not provide the confidentiality normally expected of
TLS. Protocols and applications are often designed to require confidentiality as a security
property. These cipher suites  be used in those cases.
Cipher suites marked as EXPORT use weak ciphers and were deprecated in TLS 1.1 .
Cipher suites marked as anon do not provide any authentication, are vulnerable to on-path
attacks, and were deprecated in TLS 1.1 .
RC4 is a weak cipher and is deprecated in .
DES and the International Data Encryption Algorithm (IDEA) are not considered secure for
general use and were deprecated in . MD5 and SHA-1 are also not secure for general
use and were deprecated in .
