15. Expert Review of Current and Potential IETF and IRTF
Documents
The intent of the Specification Required choice for TLS codepoints is to allow for easy
registration for codepoints associated with protocols and algorithms that are not being actively
developed inside the IETF or IRTF. When TLS-based technologies are being developed inside the
IETF or IRTF, they should be done in coordination with the TLS WG in order to provide
appropriate review. For this reason, unless the TLS WG Chairs indicate otherwise via email,
designated experts should decline codepoint registrations for documents that have already been
adopted or are being proposed for adoption by IETF working groups or IRTF research groups.
