1.3. Other Solutions
Given the consequences of LBR failures, it is also worth considering other solutions to the
problem. More specifically, power outages can be alleviated by provisioning redundant power
sources or emergency batteries. Likewise, RPL's so-called virtual DODAG roots can help tolerate
some failures of individual LBRs.
As mentioned previously, RNFD has been designed to be largely independent of those solutions;
that is, rather than aiming to be their replacement, RNFD can complement them. In particular,
the operation of RNFD with different variants of virtual DODAG roots is covered in Section 6.2.
