(either the dedicated one or RPL's original one, depending on the implementation) simply as
""Trickle timer"". In particular, a node  reset its Trickle timer when it changes its LORS to
""GLOBALLY DOWN"", so that information about the detected crash of the DODAG root is
disseminated in the DODAG fast. Likewise, a node  reset its Trickle timer when any of its
local CFRCs change significantly.
