5.4. DODAG Root's Behavior
The DODAG root node  assume the role of Acceptor in RNFD and  ever switch this
role. It  also monitor its LORS and local CFRCs, so that it can react to various events.
To start with, the DODAG root  generate a new DODAG Version, thereby restarting the
protocol, if it changes its LORS to ""GLOBALLY DOWN"", which may happen when the root has
restarted after a crash or the nodes have falsely detected its crash. It  also generate a new
DODAG Version if the fraction value(NegativeCFRC)/value(PositiveCFRC) approaches
RNFD_CONSENSUS_THRESHOLD, so as to avoid potential interruptions to routing.
Furthermore, the DODAG root  either generate a new DODAG Version or increase the bit
length of its CFRCs if saturated(PositiveCFRC) becomes TRUE. This is a self-regulation mechanism
that helps adjust the CFRCs to a potentially large number of Sentinels (see Section 6.1).
In general, issuing a new DODAG Version effectively restarts RNFD. Thus, the DODAG root 
also perform this operation in other situations.
