2.3.2. Hierarchical Names
From the outside of a specification, Given Names are usually used as part of a hierarchical name
that looks like a JSON Pointer . These hierarchical names are generally rooted in (used
as the fragment identifier in) an outer namespace that looks like an https:// URL (see Section
4).
As Quality Names and Given Names roughly alternate in a path into the model, the JSON Pointer
part of the hierarchical name also alternates between Quality Names and Given Names.
Note that the actual Given Names may need to be encoded when specified via the JSON Pointer
fragment identifier syntax. There are two layers of such encoding: tilde encoding of ~ and / as
per , as well as percent encoding of the tilde-encoded name into a valid
URI fragment as per . For example, when a model is using the Given Name
(with an embedded slash and a space) for an sdfObject, that sdfObject may need to be referenced
as
