2.4.5.7.2. Segment Routing and SRH
In a Non-Storing Mode RPL domain, the IPv6 Routing Header used for source routing is the RPL
Source Route Header as defined in . This specification operates in that context and
uses the acronym SRH to mean IPv6 RH type 3, as opposed to IPv6 RH type 4 defined in 
for Segment Routing over IPv6 (SRv6) operation.
