3.5.1. Using Storing Mode Segments
A==>B==>C and C==>D==>E are segments of the same Track. Note that the Storing Mode
signaling imposes strict continuity in a segment, since the P-DAO is passed hop by hop, as a
classical DAO is, along the reverse datapath that it signals. One benefit of strict routing is that
loops are avoided along the Track.
