Sending a packet within a RPL Local Instance requires the presence of the abstract RPI described
in  in the outer IPv6 header chain (see ). The RPI carries a Local
RPLInstanceID that, in association with either the source or the destination address in the IPv6
header, indicates the RPL Instance that the packet follows.
