4.1.7. Additional Flag in the RPL DODAG Configuration Option
The DODAG Configuration option is defined in . Its purpose is extended to
distribute configuration information affecting the construction and maintenance of the DODAG,
as well as operational parameters for RPL on the DODAG, through the DODAG. This option was
originally designed with four bit positions reserved for future use as Flags.
This specification Amends  to define the new ""Projected Routes Support"" (D) flag. The 'D'
flag is encoded in bit position 0 of the reserved Flags in the DODAG Configuration option (this is
the most significant bit). It is set to 0 in legacy implementations as specified respectively in
Sections 20.14 and 6.7.6 of .
The 'D' flag is set to 1 to indicate that this specification is enabled in the network and that the
Root will install the requested Tracks when feasible upon receiving a P-DAO-REQ message.
 Amends  to indicate that the definition of the Flags applies to
MOP values from zero (0) to six (6) only. For a MOP value of 7, the implementation 
consider that the Root accepts P-DAO-REQ messages and will install P-Routes.
