6.3. Identifying a Track
RPL defines the concept of an Instance to signal an individual routing topology, and multiple
topologies can coexist in the same network. The RPLInstanceID is tagged in the RPI of every
packet to signal which topology the packet actually follows.
This specification leverages the RPL Instance model as follows:
The main Root  use P-DAO messages to add better routes in the main Instance in
conformance with the routing objectives in that Instance.
• MAY
