DNS over CoAP (DoC)
Abstract
This document defines a protocol for exchanging DNS queries (OPCODE 0) over the Constrained
Application Protocol (CoAP). These CoAP messages can be protected by (D)TLS-Secured CoAP or
Object Security for Constrained RESTful Environments (OSCORE) to provide encrypted DNS
message exchange for constrained devices in the Internet of Things (IoT).
